# Coding Style, Chapter 1: List of style comments

The source section consists entirely of editorial and TeX coding
conventions. Its twenty numbered comments concern, respectively, line
lengths; indentation; paragraph-start commands; formula line breaking;
displayed-equation delimiters; macros; theorem-environment vocabulary;
environment layout; corollary naming; proof placement; special-file
structure; labels; cross-file references; forward references; sentence
starts; sentence endings and lead-ins; explicit hypotheses in prose; proof
length; marking defining properties; and the scope of definitions and
temporary constructions. None of these comments defines a mathematical
object or states a proposition, identity, diagram, exact sequence, example,
hypothesis, or mathematically meaningful warning. Therefore there is no
mathematical declaration to add in this file.
-/
